    "summary": "LIVE_PROBE_TOOLS is a hand-duplicated frozenset with no cross-check against GATES/mcp_gates.py or the registered tool set",
    "failure_scenario": "A future PR renames or removes one of the five live-probe tools (e.g. `profile_column` → `profile_columns`) and updates `server.py` + `mcp_gates.py`'s `GATES` together (the existing `missing = set(tools) ^ set(GATES)` check would catch that pair drifting from each other), but nobody remembers this third, independently-maintained literal in the docs generator. `groups[...]` still puts the old name in the Live-probe list, then `tools[n].description` in the row-building loop raises a bare `KeyError` for that name, since it's absent from `tools`. The CI step fails with an unrelated-looking traceback instead of the intended 'stale docs' message, and if the rename direction is instead an *addition* to the live-probe class (a new persist-nothing tool), the tool silently gets classified as an ordinary read/write in the generated docs with no error at all — the exact 'guard applied at one door and not its sibling' class this codebase has hit repeatedly (MEMORY.md: feedback_adding_a_tool_ages_its_neighbours, project_mcp_tier1_expansion)."
