    "summary": "_first_paragraph does not escape or reject markdown-table-breaking characters (`|`, embedded blank-ish separators) before interpolating a tool's docstring into a `| ... | ... | ... |` row",
    "failure_scenario": "A tool docstring's opening paragraph documents an enum or option list the way this codebase habitually does elsewhere (e.g. CLAUDE.md's own `admin | member | viewer` style) — e.g. `\"List checks of kind expectation | freshness | volume.\"`. `_first_paragraph` passes the raw text straight into the row string with no escaping, so the `|` characters split the row into extra columns, breaking the rendered mkdocs table for that tool (and potentially all rows below it, since GFM/mkdocs table parsing is sensitive to cell count per row). `--check` still passes (the generator is internally deterministic — it reproduces the same broken output on every run), so nothing in CI catches the corruption; it only surfaces as a visibly broken table on the published docs site."
