    "summary": "Paragraph-boundary detection only recognizes an exact `\\n\\n` separator, not a blank line with trailing whitespace",
    "failure_scenario": "If a tool's docstring is auto-wrapped or hand-edited so the blank line between the opening sentence and the caveat paragraph has trailing spaces (`\"...\\n   \\ncaveat text\"` instead of `\"...\\n\\ncaveat text\"`), `text.split(\"\\n\\n\", 1)` fails to find the boundary and the entire docstring (including caveat/limitation prose meant to be excluded from the one-line summary table) gets folded into the 'first paragraph' shown in the table cell — silently defeating the intended 'opening only' contract described in the module docstring, and increasing the odds of hitting the pipe-character table-break above since caveat paragraphs are more likely to contain punctuation-heavy or example text."
